# Roadmap

This roadmap reflects the current state of the project and the product direction described in `docs/PRODUCT_VISION.md`.

## Phase 0 — Foundation and project hygiene

- [ ] Document the current architecture and product direction
- [ ] Add contribution and workflow guidance
- [ ] Add environment variable documentation
- [ ] Add a test baseline and CI
- [ ] Decide on licensing

## Phase 1 — Master data and farm overview

- [ ] Improve farm/company setup and master data quality
- [ ] Clarify user roles and permissions for farms
- [ ] Improve customer and supplier master data management
- [ ] Add a global dashboard overview for key data
- [ ] Make the current `Fields` module part of the broader data model

## Phase 2 — Farm operations

- [ ] Define the first operational domain to implement (fields, crops, or contracting workflows)
- [ ] Design and prototype a minimal field / crop model
- [ ] Design and prototype a minimal contracting-services model
- [ ] Connect operational records to transactions and products

## Phase 3 — Production and stock

- [ ] Model harvest outputs and derived products
- [ ] Add stock tracking and material flow
- [ ] Support service and product billing tied to farm operations

## Phase 4 — Reporting and decision support

- [ ] Add dashboards and summaries
- [ ] Create reporting exports for customers, transactions, and farm performance
- [ ] Add AI-assisted support where it provides clear business value

## Phase 5 — Platform and business growth

- [ ] Expand to more farm profiles and more agricultural use cases
- [ ] Add accountant and multi-farm access workflows
- [ ] Improve integrations and partner ecosystem readiness
- [ ] Prepare for external data and business partnerships

## Notes

- The project is intentionally incremental.
- The product direction is ambitious, but the roadmap should remain realistic and testable.
- The current code and app separation show that the path is already moving toward domain-driven organization.

